BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(PRINCIPAL SEAT, CHENNAI\)
AT CHENNAI

CASE NO: C.S. \(Comm. Div.\) No. 104 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: MHC010345672026
DECISION DATE: 2026-03-18
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice Abdul Quddhose

PARTIES:
M/s Sundaram Technologies Private Limited
... Appellant\(s\) / Petitioner\(s\)
Versus
Aravind InfoTech LLP
... Respondent\(s\) / State

STATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:
Trade Marks Act 1999, Commercial Courts Act 2015

SECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:
Trade Marks Act Section 29, Trade Marks Act Section 134, Commercial Courts Act Section 2\(1\)\(c\)

KEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:
Trademark Infringement, Passing Off, Deceptive Similarity, Permanent Injunction, Damages

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTUAL MATRIX:
Plaintiff is the registered proprietor of trademark 'LEXGUARD' for legal software solutions. Defendant launched software under deceptively similar mark 'LEXGUARDSYS' causing confusion among judicial practitioners.

2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:
1. Whether defendant's use of 'LEXGUARDSYS' constitutes infringement under Section 29\(2\) of Trade Marks Act 1999?

3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:
Applying the doctrine of imperfect recollection and overall commercial impression as established in Cadila Healthcare.

4. RATIO DECIDENDI:
Adopting an identical prefix with minor suffix addition for identical cloud legal informatics constitutes actionable trademark infringement and passing off.

5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:
Commercial Suit Decreed; Permanent injunction granted restraining defendant from infringing registered trademark 'LEXGUARD'.

Decreed and ordered accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice Abdul Quddhose
Madras High Court \(Principal Seat, Chennai\)
[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]
) Tj ET
